# aimed.vstd: reasons aimed by the declaration curve, not by hub size.  One reason per pick of the
# greedy curve's first ten objects (tier C, tests as witnesses, name rule off, every admitted reason
# loaded): each pick needs exactly one definition with one to twelve open sites.  Each reason is what a
# developer would answer to that pick's stub; `about` names the object the curve picked (carried in the
# IR, not checked).  Some cannot be verified by this prototype: the checker's detail then names the
# machine check it lacks.

